{"title":"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281883c9645666ea3906c8689d9fb4d0a2dfd96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d544c4189ecc86c38ff791ba1b2a36563674ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{9}{14} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{5}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{7}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can first use a common denominator, and then find the value of the expression.\n</p><p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a905158a0cc49faf19f98f4bb48d78626232626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 = 2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463f0c2cdc8a7058b8337caf5cf9327c8aa166b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 = 2^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71e1d81e9d43f49171477ca6e8a8f996ddda7d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 = 2^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />. We then see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the common denominator, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a5c541e662d1983b18c81e16f2a03082296ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1 \\times 4}{2 \\times 4} = \\frac{4}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"121\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69df6b10ddf49226aebbe670ff30d40429ce10f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{3 \\times 2}{4 \\times 2} = \\frac{6}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"121\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cd1e683e0c8e4de689094ccf9896b521f7a974c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{8} = \\frac{5 \\times 1}{8 \\times 1} = \\frac{5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"121\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Thus:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a1e9478f9b937e5ea5e99f8edfc3a449f0c5c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{5}{8} = \\frac{4}{8} + \\frac{6}{8} - \\frac{5}{8} = \\frac{4 + 6 - 5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"293\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c9e0aeab5f10e18ae8c5245d86ac9502b2965b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{10 - 5}{8} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{5}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"158\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2004 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5 (page doe